  "solution": "The pattern followed here is:\n\n**Logic: (First number)² + (Third number)² = Second number.**\n\n1) (12, 313, 13)\n\n⇒ (12)² + (13)²\n\n⇒ 144 + 169 = 313\n\n2) (11, 185, 8)\n\n⇒ (11)2 + (8)2\n\n⇒ 121 + 64 = 185\n\nLet's check each option one by one:\n\n**Option 1) **(12, 158, 12)\n\n⇒ (12)2 + (12)2\n\n⇒ 144 + 144 = 288 ≠ 158. (Incorrect)\n\n**Option 2) **(4, 125, 11)\n\n⇒ (4)2 + (11)2\n\n⇒ 16 + 121 = 137 ≠ 125. (Incorrect)\n\n**Option 3) **(9, 90, 3)\n\n⇒ (9)2 + (3)2\n\n⇒ 81 + 9 = 90. (Correct)\n\n**Option 4) **(15, 150, 10)\n\n⇒ (15)2 + (10)2\n\n⇒ 225 + 100 = 325 ≠ 150. (Incorrect)\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"(9, 90, 3)\".**",
